WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:04.960
When I was younger,

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.462
I used to get told off
in class for doodling.

00:00:07.504 --> 00:00:08.880
I couldn't stop.

00:00:09.506 --> 00:00:12.842
My teacher would always
stop me from doing this,

00:00:12.884 --> 00:00:16.721
and it was really worrying
because as a creative person,

00:00:16.763 --> 00:00:18.932
it's something that I do naturally.

00:00:20.016 --> 00:00:22.686
After a few weeks at my art class,

00:00:22.686 --> 00:00:25.981
I was booked in because I was having
this trouble at school.

00:00:26.856 --> 00:00:29.568
My teacher suggested something unusual.

00:00:29.609 --> 00:00:32.779
There was a big empty wall
in a local restaurant.

00:00:33.238 --> 00:00:35.198
She asked them if I could draw on it.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:36.825
They said yes.

00:00:36.825 --> 00:00:40.161
So I started filling
the restaurant wall with my artwork.

00:00:40.704 --> 00:00:43.415
People would come in and watch me
while they were eating.

00:00:43.415 --> 00:00:45.333
Photos started appearing online.

00:00:45.709 --> 00:00:48.670
Then the local newspaper wrote about it,

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:49.879
and suddenly,

00:00:49.921 --> 00:00:52.799
people all around the world
were talking about this kid

00:00:52.841 --> 00:00:54.259
who couldn't stop doodling.

00:00:55.051 --> 00:00:56.886
That moment changed my life.

00:00:56.928 --> 00:00:58.930
I wasn't even trying to be an artist,

00:00:58.972 --> 00:01:02.017
but the important thing is how it started.

00:01:02.017 --> 00:01:06.229
It started with my imagination
and parents who didn't disregard

00:01:06.229 --> 00:01:08.106
but embraced my passion.

00:01:08.898 --> 00:01:11.067
It started with the freedom to just draw.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:14.112
And that's what I want
to talk about today,

00:01:14.112 --> 00:01:17.115
because the world is very
different than when it was

00:01:17.115 --> 00:01:19.659
when I was first doodling 10 years ago.

00:01:19.701 --> 00:01:20.827
(Laughter)

00:01:21.494 --> 00:01:24.247
Today, it's possible
to type prompts into AI,

00:01:24.289 --> 00:01:26.499
make anything and feel creative.

00:01:27.042 --> 00:01:29.085
But I believe there will always be value

00:01:29.127 --> 00:01:33.506
in letting our imaginations
be the true driver of our creations.

00:01:34.215 --> 00:01:36.551
Because imagination is like a muscle.

00:01:36.551 --> 00:01:39.095
The more you use it,
the stronger it becomes.

00:01:39.095 --> 00:01:40.513
But if you don't use it,

00:01:40.555 --> 00:01:44.517
it gets weaker and your body will rely
on something else to do it for you.

00:01:45.435 --> 00:01:47.479
Creativity is not encouraged today.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:48.897
It's not given value,

00:01:48.938 --> 00:01:52.025
so it's easy to turn
to the tools right in front of us

00:01:52.067 --> 00:01:53.526
and get an instant result.

00:01:54.152 --> 00:01:56.446
But you don't learn
by going straight to the end.

00:01:56.488 --> 00:01:57.864
You learn from the journey.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:03.244
Everything begins with a thought,
an idea, a meaning or a vision.

00:02:03.286 --> 00:02:04.871
That's your imagination.

00:02:04.913 --> 00:02:06.039
The beginning.

00:02:06.081 --> 00:02:09.000
And that beginning influences
what you do from that point.

00:02:09.042 --> 00:02:10.585
It's freedom.

00:02:10.627 --> 00:02:12.879
Imagination is the first step,

00:02:12.879 --> 00:02:15.256
and direction flows through the creation.

00:02:15.674 --> 00:02:18.593
You're letting yourself
literally wander wherever you wish.

00:02:18.635 --> 00:02:20.553
The freedom to go anywhere.

00:02:21.012 --> 00:02:23.765
Because that first step is coming from you

00:02:23.765 --> 00:02:25.475
and not something else.

00:02:25.934 --> 00:02:29.354
What I can see is we'll be reliant
to replace something

00:02:29.396 --> 00:02:31.648
we all need and all have.

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:34.734
We'll be handing it off
just because it's easier.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:36.569
And that worries me

00:02:36.569 --> 00:02:38.947
because for everyone growing up around AI,

00:02:38.947 --> 00:02:42.534
they'll see it as normal
to sacrifice their unique perspective,

00:02:42.575 --> 00:02:44.411
becoming more and more shaped,

00:02:44.411 --> 00:02:47.080
even defined, by what they can't control.

00:02:47.872 --> 00:02:50.542
I'm just going to show you
something visually now.

00:02:52.001 --> 00:02:56.339
I often start my artworks
with a simple shape.

00:02:58.591 --> 00:03:02.887
I'm thinking something spiky here.

00:03:08.226 --> 00:03:12.313
And then big eye, like this.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.610
Then I'll add some other detail.

00:03:18.862 --> 00:03:21.197
Often when I'm creating in the moment,

00:03:21.197 --> 00:03:24.367
it helps me feel very free,

00:03:24.409 --> 00:03:27.829
so I can just flow with each
character and each line.

00:03:29.956 --> 00:03:32.500
In New York, as I've traveled,

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:35.837
I've seen lots of people on skateboards,

00:03:35.879 --> 00:03:37.881
so I'm going to draw one of them.

00:03:50.018 --> 00:03:51.936
Then I'll add the wheels in there.

00:04:04.449 --> 00:04:10.330
Then I often like to add
icons, like a heart.

00:04:10.371 --> 00:04:12.916
I feel like it's very simple
but very effective.

00:04:12.957 --> 00:04:16.628
And then I love these kind of eyes,

00:04:16.628 --> 00:04:19.547
like an alien, like that.

00:04:19.547 --> 00:04:21.049
Then I'll keep this going.

00:04:21.508 --> 00:04:22.884
The arms.

00:04:25.094 --> 00:04:27.263
And then the legs as well.

00:04:35.563 --> 00:04:39.859
And with this character,
I'll just start with another simple shape.

00:04:45.824 --> 00:04:47.826
Like so, filling this.

00:04:48.535 --> 00:04:50.703
This guy's not very happy.

00:04:50.745 --> 00:04:51.913
(Laughter)

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:57.919
And then what I like to do
to balance an artwork,

00:04:57.961 --> 00:05:02.173
just add lines and shapes

00:05:02.215 --> 00:05:04.384
to just fill out the space.

00:05:14.018 --> 00:05:19.482
And movement lines,
which give life to a piece.

00:05:19.941 --> 00:05:22.610
Something I always use.

00:05:55.143 --> 00:06:01.190
(Applause)

00:06:02.108 --> 00:06:04.360
I hope we can all take a step back from AI

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:07.363
and embrace what makes us truly unique,

00:06:07.363 --> 00:06:11.075
our ability to convert
figments of our imaginations

00:06:11.075 --> 00:06:13.620
and turn them into impactful realities.

00:06:14.078 --> 00:06:16.164
We face this choice every day.

00:06:16.789 --> 00:06:20.960
So let's embrace this uniqueness,
this imagination,

00:06:21.002 --> 00:06:23.755
and the creativity
that brings us all together.

00:06:23.796 --> 00:06:24.964
Thank you.

00:06:24.964 --> 00:06:27.050
(Applause and cheers)

